The controller uses 2 RJ11 plugs to communicate with 2 controllers. We are going to use the second RJ11 jack to connect the ESP32 up to.
Protocol is RS485. 
Baud rate is 115200

There seems to be a constant keepalive on the wire, then text is sent in plain text from the main unit over the wire and button presses are sent back down the wire.

From what I can see it appears the LCD board is a dumb driver board only and all the logic is handled on the main unit.

A max485 or equivalent should do the job to get you back to TTL
RJ11 jack

RED = 12V
BLACK = GND
GREEN = RS485 A
YELLOW = RS485 B

Pinout
1 = YELLOW
2 = GREEN
3 = RED
4 = BLACK
